.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-ERS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-ers
.Nd start or renew a capsule's RFC 4998 evidence record
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis ers
.Fl -tsa Ar url ...
.Op Fl -anchor Ar der-file ...
.Op Fl -hash Ar sha256 | sha384 | sha512
.Ar dir
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A timestamp proves when a seal existed only as long as the TSA's
certificate and its hash can be trusted, a few years.
An evidence record (RFC 4998) keeps that proof for decades:
.Nm noqtis ers
writes
.Pa noqtis.ers
beside the seal of the capsule
.Ar dir
(sealed before with
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 ) ,
an EvidenceRecord whose data object is the seal file
.Pa noqtis.sig ,
byte for byte, and adds one archive timestamp to it each time it runs.
.Pp
The first run starts the record with a timestamp over the hash of the
seal file.
Each later run renews it, after the record there has been checked:
.Bl -bullet
.It
timestamp renewal, the default: a timestamp over the record's last one,
in the same chain.
Run it before the last TSA certificate expires.
.It
hash-tree renewal, with a
.Fl -hash
other than the record's: a new chain whose first timestamp covers the
seal and every chain before, with the new hash.
Run it before the record's hash weakens.
.El
.Pp
The request, the nonce and the checks on the reply are those of
.Xr noqtis-timestamp 1 ,
over the hash the next archive timestamp covers; the reply must also
not be dated before the record's last timestamp.
.Fl -tsa
may be given more than once: the TSAs are tried in order until one
gives a timestamp that checks.
.Pp
.Xr noqtis-check 1
checks the record under its
.Fl -anchor
certificates: the first timestamp must be over this seal, each next one
over the one before (or, opening a chain, over the seal and the chains
before it), and each TSA certificate valid at its own timestamp's time
and at the next one's; the last must be valid now.
While a record is there,
.Xr noqtis-seal 1
and
.Xr noqtis-timestamp 1
refuse the folder, since either would change the seal it proves.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -tsa Ar url
A time-stamping authority, as for
.Xr noqtis-timestamp 1 .
At most 32.
.It Fl -anchor Ar der-file
A TSA's root or issuing certificate, DER-encoded: the record there and
the new timestamp must verify under the anchors.
Without one, each token is checked alone and the TSA is not trusted.
At most 32.
.It Fl -hash Ar name
The new timestamp's hash:
.Cm sha256 ,
.Cm sha384
or
.Cm sha512 .
The default is the record's last one, or SHA-256 for a new record.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa dir/noqtis.ers
The evidence record, DER.
Keep it with
.Pa noqtis.sig
and
.Pa noqtis.json :
the three prove the folder as it was sealed.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
the record was written
.It 1
the record there does not check (it is not extended)
.It 2
a usage error, a folder that is not a sealed capsule, or no TSA gave a
timestamp that checks (nothing written)
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis ers --tsa http://timestamp.digicert.com results
started an evidence record for results: archive timestamp from ...
$ noqtis ers --tsa http://timestamp.digicert.com --anchor digicert.der \e
    results
renewed the evidence record's timestamp for results: ...
$ noqtis ers --tsa http://timestamp.digicert.com --anchor digicert.der \e
    --hash sha512 results
renewed the evidence record with a new hash chain for results: ...
$ noqtis check -p me.pub --anchor digicert.der results
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-timestamp 1 ,
.Xr nqersput 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%R RFC 4998
.%T Evidence Record Syntax (ERS)
.Re
.Rs
.%R RFC 3161
.%T Internet X.509 Public Key Infrastructure Time-Stamp Protocol (TSP)
.Re
